# Public Lovable Cloud connection values, committed so production builds
# always inline them. These are publishable (anon) values, safe in a bundle;
# RLS governs what they can read. Secrets never belong here.
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="ncsydqwcbtjppfgwxyvt"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://ncsydqwcbtjppfgwxyvt.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_7wn5FO6XMLFwbITSyyq6RQ_zwZeqvmW"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MAINNET CUTOVER — uncomment BOTH lines together, in one commit.
#
# Both, because they are only safe as a pair. Setting the network without the
# address gives a mainnet build with nothing to trade; setting the address
# without the network points a testnet build at a contract that has no code
# there. Either half alone trips the runtime preflight and shows visitors a
# configuration banner instead of a market.
#
# Note that plain `.env` is also loaded in production mode, so a local testnet
# override would otherwise leak into this build. That specific mistake now
# fails the build outright — see networkConsistency() in vite.config.ts.
#
# Paste the address printed by evm/deploy-testnet.sh with SHARPS_NETWORK=mainnet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_ROBINHOOD_NETWORK="mainnet"
# VITE_MARKET_ADDRESS="0x..."
